  "v1 supports Growatt only. Other manufacturers are placeholders. Hardware details: README → Supported hardware (Cloud = any Shine plant; Local = ShineWiFi-X tested, ShineLAN-X expected; X2/S not supported).": "v1 supports Growatt only. Other manufacturers are placeholders. Hardware details: README → Supported hardware (Cloud = any Shine plant; Local = ShineWiFi-X tested, ShineLAN-X expected; X2/S not supported).",
  "Why: near-realtime power from the stick (no OpenAPI delay); Shine App stays usable via cloud forward. What happens: proxy :5279 → host IP written to stick → stick reconnects here. Until step 4 succeeds, Gen24 still gets cloud data (OpenAPI) if a token is set. Undo with „Remove redirect“ (step 5 or Cloud data path). Hardware: ShineWiFi-X supported (tested); ShineLAN-X expected (same :5279 redirect, SoftAP may differ); ShineWiLan-X2 / Wifi-X2 / Wifi-S not supported.": "Why: near-realtime power from the stick (no OpenAPI delay); Shine App stays usable via cloud forward. What happens: proxy :5279 → host IP written to stick → stick reconnects here. Until step 4 succeeds, Gen24 still gets cloud data (OpenAPI) if a token is set. Undo with „Remove redirect“ (step 5 or Cloud data path). Hardware: ShineWiFi-X supported (tested); ShineLAN-X expected (same :5279 redirect, SoftAP may differ); ShineWiLan-X2 / Wifi-X2 / Wifi-S not supported.",
  "Built for ShineWiFi-X (:5279 / SoftAP :5280). ShineLAN-X may work the same way (untested here). X2 sticks and ShineWiFi-S are not supported on this path.": "Built for ShineWiFi-X (:5279 / SoftAP :5280). ShineLAN-X may work the same way (untested here). X2 sticks and ShineWiFi-S are not supported on this path.",
  "Supported target: Primo/Symo GEN24 only (not Datamanager 2.0 / older Symo without Gen24 components UI). Technician login required (Customer cannot add meters). On the Gen24 web UI: Device configuration → Components → Add component. Type: Fronius Smart Meter (TCP). IP = ioBroker IP below, Port 502, Modbus address = same as here (default 3, never 1 = primary). Application: Producer meter (Erzeugerzähler), Category: Inverter; leave the rest default. Then search Fronius below so this adapter knows the master. No physical Fronius Smart Meter is required.": "Supported target: Primo/Symo GEN24 only (not Datamanager 2.0 / older Symo without Gen24 components UI). Technician login required (Customer cannot add meters). On the Gen24 web UI: Device configuration → Components → Add component. Type: Fronius Smart Meter (TCP). IP = ioBroker IP below, Port 502, Modbus address = same as here (default 3, never 1 = primary). Application: Producer meter (Erzeugerzähler), Category: Inverter; leave the rest default. Then search Fronius below so this adapter knows the master. No physical Fronius Smart Meter is required.",
